; `mul' is the low half of a 16x16 product from a hardware multiplier - the
; iCE40 UP5K's DSPs - and `mulhu' and `mulhs' the high half.  A part without
; one has none of them, so it is off unless asked for, and libgcc, built
; without it, runs on either.
mmul
Target Mask(MUL)
Use the mul, mulhu and mulhs instructions, which need a hardware multiplier.

; How a function reaches zero page data - variables with the zp attribute.
; See `The zero page' in fructus.cc.
mzp-base=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(fructus_zp_base) Var(fructus_zp_base) Init(1)
-mzp-base=[auto|always|never]	Reach zero page variables through a base register holding 0x200: when the function's references favour it, always, or never.

Enum
Name(fructus_zp_base) Type(int)

EnumValue
Enum(fructus_zp_base) String(never) Value(0)

EnumValue
Enum(fructus_zp_base) String(auto) Value(1)

EnumValue
Enum(fructus_zp_base) String(always) Value(2)
